                <pb facs="0674" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.00/6097: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-08T11:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 9—7:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>14. My 6, January 7, 11 a.m. I am informed that British Admiralty will supply
                    necessary coal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
